================================================================================
Upstream and third-party components
================================================================================

Glasscode is built on GPUI, the UI framework of the Zed editor. We are grateful
to the Zed team and contributors.

  GPUI and its supporting crates — https://github.com/zed-industries/zed
    Copyright 2022 - 2025 Zed Industries, Inc. Licensed under Apache-2.0.
    The crates under `vendor/` (gpui, gpui_apple, gpui_macos, gpui_macros,
    gpui_platform, gpui_shared_string, gpui_util, gpui_windows, bench_metrics,
    collections, http_client, path, perf, refineable, scheduler, sum_tree, util,
    util_macros, zlog, ztracing, ztracing_macro) are copies of Zed's Apache-2.0
    crates; each keeps its LICENSE-APACHE file. Glasscode has changed some of
    them: the changes are listed in `vendor/CHANGES.md`. Glasscode takes no
    code from the parts of Zed that are under the GPL or the AGPL.

  Rust packages from crates.io, each under its own licence. The installer and
  the zip have the text of each in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.html; `about.toml`
  lists the licences a package may have.

  Fonts in `crates/glasscode/assets/fonts`, each with its licence file there:
    Geist, Geist Mono, JetBrains Mono, Inter, IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono,
    all under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.

  The names and marks of Claude, Codex, GitHub, Linear and other services belong
  to their owners and are shown only to name those services.

The glasses companion app and the voice helper additionally build on:

  Meta Wearables Device Access Toolkit (DAT) for iOS
    https://github.com/facebook/meta-wearables-dat-ios — not open source: used
    under the Meta Wearables Developer Terms
    (https://wearables.developer.meta.com/terms). Glasscode's licence does not
    cover it.

  LiveKit Swift SDK — https://github.com/livekit/client-sdk-swift
    Copyright 2023 LiveKit, Inc. Licensed under Apache-2.0.

  LiveKit FFI — https://github.com/livekit/livekit-ffi-xcframework
    Licensed under Apache-2.0.

  WebRTC, as LiveKit builds it — https://github.com/livekit/webrtc-xcframework
    Copyright (c) 2011, The WebRTC project authors. BSD 3-Clause licence;
    LiveKit's packaging of it under the MIT licence.

  Swift NIO, Swift NIO SSH, Swift Crypto and their supporting packages —
    https://github.com/apple — Licensed under Apache-2.0.

The Mac app also carries LiveKit's server (livekit-server,
https://github.com/livekit/livekit), Copyright 2023 LiveKit, Inc., licensed
under Apache-2.0, for the manager's voice on the Mac.

The full licence texts and notices of these packages, at the versions built,
are in voice/helper/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt (the Mac app) and
glasses/GlasscodeGlasses/Sources/Licenses/ThirdPartyNotices.txt (the glasses
app, which shows them in Settings › Licences); script/swift-notices.py writes
both. The Rust packages' licences go with the programs as
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.html (cargo-about).

The voice worker (voice/manager/worker) installs LiveKit Agents and its plugins
(Apache-2.0) when it runs; they are not part of what Glasscode ships. The
speech services those plugins reach are used with each person's own account,
under that service's terms.

Other dependencies are declared in Cargo.toml / Cargo.lock (Rust), in the
Swift package manifests, and in voice/manager/worker/requirements.txt (the
voice worker, Python), each under its own licence.

================================================================================

Glasscode depends on no hosted service of its own. Off-network access is
provided by Tailscale (recommended) or an optional self-hosted relay.
